From 1ab4cad1c9ad9ac5d875803bc8645335683182a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:55:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libva: Restore export_include_dirs on the libva shared
 library

Removing export_include_dirs: ["."] dropped the source-tree include
root that consumers linking against libva used to get for free via
<va/va.h> and other public headers. Exporting generated_headers does
not substitute for that root, and a dependency on libva_headers only
propagates its headers to a consumer if that consumer explicitly
re-exports or separately depends on it.

Every current consumer in this tree (media-driver, cmrtlib, the
onevpl examples, mediasdk_c2's c2_components) already depends on
libva_headers directly, so none of them broke -- but restore the
self-export anyway so libva keeps working for any future consumer
that depends on it the way it used to.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 Android.bp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index debff8d..eac99ac 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -94,6 +94,10 @@ cc_library_shared {
         "va"
     ],
 
+    export_include_dirs: [
+        ".",
+    ],
+
     generated_headers: [
         "libva_gen_version",
     ],
-- 
2.34.1

